From 167f743397a581eeada6dbc752cb6f7b3a3d111c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mattromano <mattromano88@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 05:41:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(audio): real-time pitch shift on the backing bus
 (Auto-Tuner B)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a tempo-preserving live-retune shifter to the backing-track render
path so a physically detuned guitar can play along, driven by the
Auto-Tuner plugin via IPC (added next). Runtime only — no DLC writes.

- vendor signalsmith-stretch (MIT, header-only) as a submodule pinned to
  tag 1.0.0, which bundles its own dsp/ headers (no transitive deps)
- BackingPitchShifter: pImpl wrapper confining the heavy template to one
  TU. prepare()/reset() allocate (off the audio thread); setSemitones()
  and process() are RT-safe (atomics, no locks, no allocation). 0 st =
  early-return bypass so normal playback stays bit-untouched.
- AudioEngine: configure in audioDeviceAboutToStart(), process the
  backing block in place before the mix, reset on seek. While a shift is
  active, report the backing position minus the shifter latency so the
  chart playhead stays aligned with the (delayed) audio. Expose
  set/getBackingPitchSemitones + getBackingPitchLatencyMs.
- CMake: add BackingPitchShifter.cpp + the signalsmith include dir.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mattromano <mattromano88@gmail.com>
